  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Fund to Fight AIDS TB and Malaria Set-Aside for Financial Years 2023-24 to 2025-26</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This investment includes activities that contribute to Australia&apos;s $26.6 million &apos;set-aside&apos; from its 7th replenishment pledge to the Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria. The set-aside is managed by Australia to support Global Fund objectives in the Indo-Pacific. The investment includes two projects funded as part of the Partnerships for a Healthy Region competitive call for projects (with partners UNAIDS/ Health Equity Matters; and the Centre for Community Health Research and Development) as well as additional activities not included in the PHR competitive call, for technical assistance such as support to country coordinating mechanisms (CCMs) and grant writing support. Further projects that also contribute to Australia&apos;s Global Fund set aside are included in other separate investments.</narrative>
  </description>
